WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.360
Hi, welcome back to the Wheel of Life home retreat.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.640
Today my translator is Allison Zhou.
Thank you for coming.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.080
Session fourteen is called "Contact with the Outside."

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:35.920
And the image we're using is a bunch of kids
looking out a window with a telescope.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.480
And this kind of represents all the parts of your mind

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.680
making their first contact with the outside.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:56.480
So, where have we come in the Wheel of Life so far?

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:07.440
We have link number one:
you misunderstand your husband, you say,
"I didn't do anything--he yelled at me!"

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:17.320
Then step number two: you make karma
because you don't understand him.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:26.800
"I'm not stupid, you're stupid!"
Then that karma is impressed onto the mind.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.440
You carry that mind to your next life,

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.160
it enters the womb--

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:42.280
it enters the blood and the semen.
In Tibetan, it's called the blood and the semen.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:49.280
And I've been calling it menstrual blood and semen,

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:57.040
but of course we understand--
now that we have microscopes--

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:04.520
that it's really the semen and the seed
of the mother, which is in the blood.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:15.040
Okay, then the mind enters
that substance--those substances--

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:23.640
at link number three, which is called "consciousness," and it's the monkey entering the womb.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:29.800
Link number three, which is called "consciousness," but it's the monkey entering the womb.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:40.320
Andn then we talked already about link number four,

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.800
which is basically your body and your mind developing inside the womb.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.520
And now we reach link number five.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:58.520
Don't forget why we are learning all of these links--

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:03.960
these are the steps in the process that trigger each other.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:12.520
And they're how we get in trouble.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:17.120
If you're in this Wheel,

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.680
you are having trouble in your life--

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.760
you will live and you will die.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:30.240
And the goal of learning all these links,

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.960
is to learn how to stop them.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.160
It doesn't mean we disappear.

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.680
Nirvana doesn't mean you disappear;

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:47.520
it just means your life changes

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:53.720
into a perfect life where you
cannot die and you cannot get old.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:59.160
Okay, so we've reached link number five.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:03.320
In Tibetan, it's called ngapa kye che (LNGA PA SKYE MCHED).

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:09.880
And what it means is the "[five] doors of sense."

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:15.200
Let's go to the text:

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:21.840
ngapa kye che kyi tendrel ni
(LNGA PA SKYE MCHED KYI RTEN 'BREL NI)
So what is the link that we call number five?

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:27.760
And these are the organs of sense.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:33.120
mik na sok kyi kye che druk druppa ne sung
(MIG RNA SOGS KYI SKYE MCHED DRUG GRUB PA NAS BZUNG)

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:44.680
So this link goes from the time that your instruments for experiencing the world are developing, like your eye, and your ear.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:57.120
So it's like the Heart Sutra:
mik me, nawa med, na me, che me, lu me, yi me, suk me
(MIG MED, RNA BA MED, SNA MED, LCE MED, LUS MED, YID MED, GZUGS MED)

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:12.360
It goes: eyes, ears, nose, tongue, skin, and then mind.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:18.720
So your mind is also one of your sense organs.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:24.480
Okay, so he says "six sense organs" here.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:35.760
So once you have an eye, you can start
to experience the outside world.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:50.040
That experience begins when the eye meets the object, which meets the mind behind the eye.
Those three things.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:03.200
So, so far, we aren't yet able to experience
the details of the object.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:10.640
We do have an eye, we do have a nose
we do have an ear ...

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:19.160
but they are like empty houses,
and that's the image in the link here.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:24.120
Nobody's looking out the window yet.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:30.440
So first, those sense faculties have to develop,

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:36.040
and then you can look out through them.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:51.240
lu dang yi kyi wangpo ni mer merpoy kap ne yupar sung
(LUS DANG YID KYI DBANG PO NI MER MER PO'I SKABS NAS YOD PAR GSUNGS,)--
it is stated that even from the time that your consciousness enters that messy blood and semen,

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:00.120
you don't yet have eyes.

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:06.000
But traditionally, they say

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:10.000
from that first few minutes inside your mom,

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:14.960
when your mind enters those liquids,

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:20.840
you do have this sense power of thought

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:29.360
and you do have a kind of skin--it's just scum right now.

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:39.280
dzu kye tabur kam okma nyi su ming suk kyi tendrel dang, kye che kyi tendrel chik char du drup
(RDZUS SKYES LTA BUR KHAMS 'OG MA GNYIS SU MING GZUGS KYI RTEN 'BREL DANG, SKYE MCHED KYI RTEN 'BREL CIG CAR DU 'GRUB,)

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:43.560
Now there's a special kind of birth in Buddhism,

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:54.280
and certain special people are just born in a second, complete--inside a lotus for example.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:06.080
Like this big ... and then in one second,
they're like "pop" and they're a whole person.

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:12.160
So in the lower two realms--
desire realm and form--

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:24.120
they say that the name and form ... the two parts of body and mind, in the womb--

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:31.800
the two parts: body and mind, inside the womb.

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:37.000
And this link, which is number five--link number five,

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:39.960
your sense organs--

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:43.800
if you are born miraculously,

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:48.480
those all happen at the same time.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:54.480
So there's no distinction between the body
in the womb and the body outside the womb.

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:03.360
suk me la ming gi tendrel dang, yi kyi kye che kyi tendrel tsam le suk dang ky che suk chen ngay tendrel med
(GZUGS MED LA MING GI RTEN 'BREL DANG, YID KYI SKYE MCHED KYI RTEN 'BREL TZAM LAS GZUGS DANG SKYE MCHED GZUGS CAN LNGA'I RTEN 'BREL MED)--

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:09.280
when you're talking about a person who is
being born into the formless realm,

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:20.000
they don't have the name of 'name and form,"
because the name... I'm sorry ...

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:26.120
I'm sorry ... they don't have the form part;
they just have the name part--just a mental part.

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:35.040
yid kyi kye che kyi tendrel (YIK KYI SKYE MCHED KYI RTEN 'BREL)--
they have the sense organ of the thought,

00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:39.960
but they don't have the others--the other five:
the eyes, and ears, and nose...

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:47.120
That finishes his presentation of the sense organs.

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:51.960
nga pa kye che

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:55.240
Yeah, the [Chinese] of number five.

00:09:56.880 --> 00:10:02.800
Okay, we've link number six reached,

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:07.040
which is called "contact."

00:10:08.360 --> 00:10:15.840
And here's the description ... it's not very long.
By the way, the image is a man touching a woman,

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:23.400
and this link does not refer to sex or something like that--

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:30.200
it's a different kind of contact.
So the painting is just a metaphor.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:37.840
drukpa rekpa ni (DRUG PA REG PA NI)--link number six is called "contact."

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:42.400
So now the sense organs have formed

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:49.400
and three things make contact.

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:56.280
Okay, here's your eye, for example--the eye power.

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:02.320
Then here's a red apple,

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:08.800
and then here's the awareness of the red apple.

00:11:10.280 --> 00:11:18.960
So when the eye sees the red,
and the mind is aware of the red,

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:23.560
when these three make contact,

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:26.960
we call it "contact."

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:30.720
So here in the text it says:

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:37.680
yul wangpo namshe sum tre
(YUL DBANG PO RNAM SHES GSUM 'PHRAD)--
The object (the red apple),

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:45.440
the sense power (the eye),
and the awareness (of the red apple),

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:54.000
they meet each other and that's called "contact."

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:57.280
Okay, after contact ...

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:03.800
then, how should we say ... by the way, during contact... sorry ...

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:17.200
I'm going to change that.
That contact up to the time that you are able to distinguish,

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:24.000
"Oh, this is something nice, this is not something nice,"

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:29.400
that period of contact has been made,

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:35.040
but you're not feeling anything yet.

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:42.640
That link is called number six, "contact."

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:47.480
Okay, now that causes number seven.

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:52.120
Link number seven, which is called dunpa tsorwa (BDUN PA TSOR BA).

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:55.400
dunpa (BDUN PA) means link number "seven,"

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:58.400
tsorwa (TSOR BA) means "feelings."

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:03.320
Here's the definition: dunpa tsor ba ni ...

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:09.160
rekpay kyen gyi tsowar de duk tang nyom sum chi rik kyewa te
(REG PA'I RKYEN GYIS TSOR BA BDE SDUG BTANG SNYOMS GSUM CI RIGS SKYE BA STE)--

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:15.960
Because the mind, and the sense power,
and the object make contact,

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:26.720
then you can start to say, "Oh, I like apples,"
or, "I'm allergic to apples."

00:13:28.520 --> 00:13:32.520
And you can feel happy or you can feel sad,

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.680
and that's called feeling.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:45.160
The traditional picture is a very terrible kind of feeling--the man has an arrow in his eye,

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:52.080
and it's just an extreme example of feeling.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:58.360
Of course, he's feeling intense pain.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:03.040
Now what kinds of feeling are there?

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:06.120
de duk tang nyom
(BDE SDUG BTANG SNYOMS).

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:09.960
de (BDE) means a "nice feeling."

00:14:10.400 --> 00:14:13.480
duk (SDUG) means duk ngel (SDUG BSNGAL) means "pain."

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:19.200
tang nyom (BTANG SNYOMS) means
"I don't feel good, I don't feel bad"--

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:22.080
just "neutral feeling.:

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:26.040
chi rik kyewa te (CI RIGS SKYE BA STE)--as soon as there is contact,

00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:31.280
one of those feelings will come up.

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:37.280
Now usually we would say, "How are you feeling?"

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:46.040
In English we say,
"Well, I'm not feeling anything right now."

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:56.160
"I don't enjoy this thing, I don't dislike this thing--I'm just kind of not feeling anything right now."

00:14:57.560 --> 00:15:03.440
But in Buddhist philosophy, you are always feeling something.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:12.360
The feeling might be neutral,
but you are still having a feeling.

00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:17.040
Once there's contact with the outside world,

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:21.440
or even hearing your own thoughts, you

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:25.000
will start to feel something.

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:30.200
And one of the kinds of suffering in this world

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:34.560
is that you cannot turn those feelings off.

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:42.440
When I first started to teach in New York,
maybe 35 years ago,

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:47.160
I used to interview every student.

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:56.080
And I didn't have time, I used to interview them--because I was working full-time at the diamond business--

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:02.240
so I would meet people at lunchtime.

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:15.160
And I distinctly remember meeting this person ... it was on Fifth Avenue, and we had lunch together.

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:21.040
And I said, "What do you do for a living?"

00:16:22.760 --> 00:16:26.920
And he said, "I steal things--I'm a robber."

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:34.560
Then suddenly I got nervous,
I started holding my phone like... I said, "Oh ... oh, really?"

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:39.000
"Yeah, I break into people's houses."

00:16:40.400 --> 00:16:44.520
I'm surprised. I said, "Well, why do you do that?"

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:48.080
He said "I'm a heroin addict."

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:56.120
Then I was like, "What?" He said, "I'm a heroin addict.
I shoot heroin. I need money."

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:03.440
Then I'm thinking, "Oh, this guy cannot come into our school,  he will steal everything."

00:17:06.760 --> 00:17:10.320
But something came in my mind.

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:16.080
I said, "I never tried heroin."

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:21.560
I said, "Why do you do that? Why do you take heroin?"

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:26.680
He said, "I want to stop feeling things.

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:35.040
I don't care if it's a good feeling or a bad feeling, I don't want any feeling.

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:38.200
I don't want to kill myself,

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:43.680
because I'm afraid--I don't know what will happen.

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:47.040
But I'm tired of feeling things,

00:17:47.640 --> 00:17:50.600
it's too much for me.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:54.320
Just after I take the heroin,

00:17:55.400 --> 00:18:00.120
then for an hour or two hours, I don't feel anything."

00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:05.680
Actually, so what we have to say,
according to this, he is feeling things.

00:18:08.640 --> 00:18:11.200
It's neutral feeling.

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:18.000
We are always feeling, and that's one of the
sufferings of the Wheel of Life.

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:23.040
You cannot stop feeling.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:27.840
My little brother committed suicide.

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:37.280
And he was very intelligent, he was strong, and handsome ... twenty years old.

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:46.120
But he said, "I just want to stop feeling."
And he killed himself.

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:50.360
Now unfortunately, in the Wheel of Life

00:18:52.040 --> 00:18:56.280
even if you shoot the brain, which he did,

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:06.840
you cannot stop the life--the mind is still alive.

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:12.560
And the mind will not die, and the mind
will go to another place,

00:19:13.800 --> 00:19:19.800
and it will go through another circle, and you will have feeling--it won't stop for one second.

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:26.000
So we need to find another way out of the Wheel.

00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:32.760
And that's why we are studying the Wheel.

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:37.160
So we'll see you again in session fifteen.

00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:41.640
We're going to find out...

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:46.320
... so after you plant the seed,

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:51.600
what makes the seed start growing?

00:19:53.560 --> 00:19:55.560
[Allison]: Start or stop? [Geshe Michael]:  Start.

00:19:57.480 --> 00:20:03.040
And we're going to talk about that in session fifteen.
See you then.

